{100}{}{(A wiry man with a pipe and a smile that doesn't reach his eyes.) Tyler says the Gutter's been busy. People coming in at night, going out south. Metzger pays Tyler to notice things like that. Tyler figures you'll pay more for him to stop noticing.}
{101}{}{[Barter] Four hundred, and Tyler forgets the whole thing. Take it or leave with nothing.}
{102}{}{[Speech] Lara's been asking about the church again. Maybe Tyler should worry about that instead of me.}
{103}{}{[Speech] Metzger's finished, Deke. Tell Tyler to ride with the side that's still standing next year.}
{104}{}{Get out of my house.}
{105}{}{I'll think about it.}
{106}{}{Get out!}
{110}{}{(He counts it twice.) Pleasure. Tyler's eyes are bad lately. Getting worse every day.}
{111}{}{...}
{120}{}{(Deke goes pale.) The church. Right. Tyler's going to want to hear about that. You didn't see me here.}
{130}{}{(He chews on it for a long time.) Metzger's old. Lara's young. And you've got the Rangers on a string. Tyler's not stupid. When it happens, we'll be looking the other way. Maybe even your way.}
{140}{}{(Deke whistles. Boots on the stairs.) Wrong answer.}
{141}{}{Come on, then.}
{150}{}{You'll bleed for this.}

